msgstr "Telegram login was cancelled."

msgid "telegram.error"
msgstr "Telegram login failed, please try again."

msgid "telegram.already-linked"
msgstr "This Telegram account is already connected to another volunteer."

msgid "telegram.not-on-list"
msgstr "Your Telegram username isn't on the volunteer list. Please contact the volunteer coordinators."

msgid "telegram.admin.title"
msgstr "Telegram & bot"

msgid "telegram.admin.import_shifts.title"
msgstr "Create the shifts"

msgid "telegram.admin.import_shifts.info"
msgstr "Before the volunteer import, as it puts people on these shifts. Paste CSV rows: title, area, location, start, end, needed. Start and end look like \"2027-08-17 08:00\" (the site's time zone), needed is the number of people for the area, leads included. Missing locations are created, and each shift gets a shift type named after its area. A shift that already exists (same title, start, end and location) is reused: a missing area is added, a lower need is raised."

msgid "telegram.admin.import_shifts"
msgstr "Create shifts"

msgid "telegram.admin.import.title"
msgstr "Import the final volunteer list"

msgid "telegram.admin.import.info"
msgstr "Do this once, when the list is final and the shifts exist. Paste CSV rows: handle, name, area, shifts, lead. Shifts look like \"2027-08-17 AM; 2027-08-18 PM\"; a shift in another area names it, like \"2027-08-19 AM Kitchen\". Lead is \"yes\" for leads of the area, or the areas they lead, like \"Info Desk; Kitchen\". Each row creates an account with areas, lead role and shifts. People who already have an account only get their areas, lead role and shifts added; nothing else changes."

msgid "telegram.admin.import"
msgstr "Import"

